2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kai_Donner '''Karl (Kai) Reinhold Donner'''] (1888–1935) was a Finnish linguist, ethnographer and politician. He carried out expeditions to the Nenets people (Samoyeds) in Siberia 1911–1914 and was d
2 CONC ocent of Uralic languages at the University of Helsinki from 1924. He was, among other things, a pioneer of modern anthropological fieldwork methods, though his work is little known in the English-speaking world.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://fi.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kai_Donner '''Karl Reinhold (Kai) Donner'''] (1888–1935) oli suomalainen suomalais-ugrilaisiin kieliin erikoistunut kielitieteilijä ja antropologi sekä itsenäisyys- ja oikeistoaktivisti.
2 CONT
