1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carl_August_Adlersparre
2 CONT
2 CONT https://sok.riksarkivet.se/SBL/Presentation.aspx?id=5562
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Adlersparre_nr_130#TAB_2
2 CONT
2 CONT Life[edit]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the oldest son of Georg Adlersparre (1760-1835) and Lovisa Magdalena Linroth (April 20, 1784 - November 8, 1866 Kristinehamn Municipality, Värmland). As a student he pursue the military career and in 1841 became lieutenant 
2 CONC in the Värmland field Hunters Regiment , but took leave in 1845. In 1848 he married Charlotte Aurore Jeanette von Platen (1821-1853) who bore him a daughter, Louise Henrietta Adlersparre (1850-1875).[1] He died in Stockholm, aged 
2 CONC almost 52.
2 CONT
2 CONT Work[edit]
2 CONT
2 CONT He wrote poem and novels in the romantic style but without deep motivation. For these efforts he was awarded five minor Swedish academic prices (1834–43). Here is a selection of his poems:[2] (Swedish) Ungdoms-dikter (Youth Poems)
2 CONC , Förf., Stockholm, 1830 [3] (Swedish) Hugo: en romantisk dikt (Hugo, a romantic poem), Carlstad, 1840 [4] (Swedish) Smärre samlade dikter (Minor collected poems), Carlstad, 1841 [5]
2 CONT
2 CONT In prose he wrote, among others:[2] (Swedish) Skizzer och reseminnen (Sketches and Travel Memories), 1844 (Swedish) Smärre skizzer (Minor Sketches) in 2 volumes, Albert Bonniers, Stockholm, 1849-50[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT He is mostly remembered for his historical biographies:[2] (Swedish) 1809 års revolution och dess män (The 1809 revolution and its men), 2 vol., Stockholm, 1849, Albert Bonniers Föorlag (Swedish) 1809 Och 1810: Tidstaflor, 3 vol.,
2 CONC  Stockholm, 1850, Albert Bonniers Föorlag[7] (Swedish) Anteckningar om bortgångne samtida, 3 vol., Stockholm 1860-1862, Albert Bonniers
