1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Med. dr. Professor i obstetrik.
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://runeberg.org/nornan/1889/0180.html '''Svensk Kalender 1889 6.e årgången'''] '''Nils Vilhelm Netzel''' gynekolog och operatör, professor i obstetrik och öfverläkare vid Stockholms allmänna barnbördshus, föddes den 1 novem
2 CONC ber 1834 i Stockholm, der fadern '''Nils Gustaf Netzel''' var grosshandlare; modern '''Hedda Wilhelmina Sandblad'''. Sedan hangenomgått Vesterås läroverk, blef han student i Upsala 1853 och promoverades efter afslutade medicinska 
2 CONC studier 1865 till medicine doktor. Sin verksamhet som gynekolog och obstetriker började prof. Netzel såsom amanuens vid den obstetriska kliniken å allmänna barnbördshuset 1863, blef 1864 tillförordnad adjunkt i gynekologi och obst
2 CONC etrik, ordinarie adjunkt vid karolinska institutet 1864 och utnämdes efter professor Andersons afgång till professor i obstetrik och gynekologi. Under åren 1862, 1868 till 1869 och vid senare tillfällen har prof. Netzel vistats i 
2 CONC utlandet i och för gynekologiska studier. Gift med '''Laura Constance Pistolekors''', född 1839 i Finland. Från trycket har professor Netzel utgifvit bland annat en afhandling: Om de puerperala förändringarna inom lifmodern samt l
2 CONC emnat meddelanden om af honom utförda ovariotomier.
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wilhelm_Netzel '''Wikipedia: Nils Wilhelm Netzel'''] (1 November 1834 – 7 February 1914) was a Swedish gynecologist and obstetrician.
2 CONT * '''Biography'''
2 CONT * Netzel was born in Stockholm and studied at Uppsala University, completing his dissertation in 1865 on puerperal changes in modern life. In 1863 he took a position as assistant in the obstetric department at the General Maternit
2 CONC y Hospital in Stockholm. In 1864 he became a substitute lecturer in obstetrics and gynecology at the Karolinska Institute, and in 1865 became a regular lecturer and in 1879, a professor. In 1887 he succeeded Anders Anderson as pro
2 CONC fessor of obstetrics and gynecology and retained this position until 1889.[1] He performed his first ovariotomy in 1869 and later published numerous studies, providing important research for development of medical procedures. In 1
2 CONC 904 he was elected an honorary member of the Swedish Society of Medicine. He died in Stockholm.
2 CONT * In 1866 Netzel married Swedish composer and music conductor '''Laura Netzel neé Pistolekors''' born in Finland. He maintained a herbarium which was donated on his death to the University of Stockholm. A biography of his life was
2 CONC  published in 1914 by Frans Johan Eugène Westermark.
