2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Adolf Karlovich Etolin, lso Arvid Adolf Etholén, (January 9, 1798 - March 29, 1876) was a naval officer, explorer and administrator who was employed by the Russian-American Company. He was a Finn, born in Helsinki, Finland. Etholé
2 CONC n first reached Sitka in the service of the Russian-American Company in 1818, rising to Chief Manager of the Company 1840-1845 (Chief Manager was a position sometimes referred to, though incorrectly, as Governor).
2 CONT
